.\" man/man3/Docv::Fuzzy.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Fuzzy" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Fuzzy \- Fuzzy matching of a query against text, scored like fzf.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Fuzzy\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Fuzzy matching of a query against text, scored like fzf. The query\(aqs
characters must appear in the text in order; a match scores higher at
word starts, in runs of consecutive characters and with short gaps. The
best alignment is found by dynamic programming over the window between
the first possible start and the last possible end.
.PP
A query in lower case matches case\-insensitively; a query with an
upper\-case letter matches exactly.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
fuzzy = Docv::Fuzzy.new("prf")
fuzzy.score("printf")     # => 73
fuzzy.positions("printf") # => [0, 1, 5]
fuzzy.score("open")       # => nil
.EE
.RE
.PP
A matcher reuses its buffers between calls; use one per fiber.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBASCII\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ASCII = StaticArray(Kind, 128).new do |code| Fuzzy.kind(code.unsafe_chr) end
.EE
.RE
.PP
Class of every ASCII character.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBBONUS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BONUS = Kind.values.map do |previous| Kind.values.map do |current| Fuzzy.bonus(previous, current) end end
.EE
.RE
.PP
\fB\%BONUS[previous][current]\fR: the bonus of a character of class
\fIcurrent\fR following one of class \fIprevious\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBBONUS_BOUNDARY = SCORE_MATCH // 2\fR
.PP
\fBBONUS_CAMEL = BONUS_BOUNDARY + GAP_EXTENSION\fR
.PP
\fBBONUS_CONSECUTIVE = \-(GAP_START + GAP_EXTENSION)\fR
.PP
\fBBONUS_DELIMITER = BONUS_BOUNDARY + 1\fR
.PP
\fBBONUS_NON_WORD = SCORE_MATCH // 2\fR
.PP
\fBBONUS_WHITE = BONUS_BOUNDARY + 2\fR
.TP 4
\fBDELIMITERS = {\(aq/\(aq, \(aq,\(aq, \(aq:\(aq, \(aq;\(aq, \(aq|\(aq}\fR
Characters after which a word starts with \fB\%BONUS_DELIMITER\fR.
.PP
\fBFIRST_CHAR_MULTIPLIER = 2\fR
.PP
\fBGAP_EXTENSION = \-1\fR
.PP
\fBGAP_START = \-3\fR
.TP 4
\fBNONE = Int32::MIN // 2\fR
Score of an impossible alignment.
.PP
\fBSCORE_MATCH = 16\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(query : String)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.bonus(previous : Kind, current : Kind) : Int32\fR
The bonus of a \fIcurrent\fR character after a \fIprevious\fR one: word
starts, camel humps and digits after non\-digits, and non\-word
characters themselves.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.kind(char : Char) : Kind\fR
The class of \fIchar\fR.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef empty? : Bool\fR
True for an empty query, which matches everything with score 0.
.TP 4
\fBdef exact? : Bool\fR
True when the query has upper case and matches exactly.
.TP 4
\fBdef match?(text : Bytes) : Bool\fR
True when the query is a subsequence of the UTF\-8 \fItext\fR, under the
same case rule as \fB\%score\fR: what \fB\%score\fR finds a match in, without
aligning. Used to count matching lines in bulk (\fB\%Corpus\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef positions(text : String) : Array(Int32) | Nil\fR
The character indices of the best alignment in \fItext\fR; \fB\%nil\fR when
there is no match.
.PP
\fBdef query : String\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef score(text : String) : Int32 | Nil\fR
The score of the best alignment of the query in \fItext\fR; \fB\%nil\fR when the
query is not a subsequence of it.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/fuzzy.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Corpus" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Fuzzy::Kind" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
